                        "glosses": [
                            "A biography that highlights the negative aspects of its subject's life."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "48b1a613-1fd7-4d0c-8dbb-39d49744ef4e",
                                "sense_id": "39880d2d-c5ba-3905-8f0b-6999e1b9e883",
                                "text": "Though this has been an era of magisterial biographies by such writers as Leon Edel, Richard Ellmann, Joseph Frank, Judith Thurman and Justin Kaplan, among others, it has also evolved a new subspecies of the genre to which the name \"pathography\" might usefully be given: hagiography's diminished and often prurient twin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3712de0e-a787-4e70-a06e-cc9510893f84",
                                "sense_id": "39880d2d-c5ba-3905-8f0b-6999e1b9e883",
                                "text": "One would think there is little to be added, if only because of the avalanche of books — biographies, meta-biographies, pathographies (to borrow Joyce Carol Oates’s term), memoirs, critical studies, letters, journals, novels — that have been published about Plath since her suicide (which, for some people, is the only thing they know about her)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
